     kkeeyyllooggiinn — decrypt and store secret key

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     kkeeyyllooggiinn

DDEEPPRREECCAATTIIOONN NNOOTTIICCEE
     kkeeyyllooggiinn is deprecated and is not available as of FreeBSD 15.0.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkeeyyllooggiinn utility prompts the user for their login password, and uses
     it to decrypt the user's secret key stored in the publickey(5) database.
     Once decrypted, the user's key is stored by the local key server process
     keyserv(8) to be used by any secure network services, such as NFS.

